00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:21.740
Can individual authors edit their past records
to include ORCID IDs?

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:28.700
It by record you are saying PubMed citations,
no authors cannot, publishers can.

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:33.190
Honestly if you reach out to a publisher,
and either they are no longer -- it has to

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:37.480
be the publisher, the active data provider
for that journal, that is another thing that

00:17:37.480 --> 00:17:43.549
switches a lot is data for a journal once
submitted by High Wire, might be submitted

00:17:43.549 --> 00:17:50.240
by Elsevier or by a third-party vendor. We
always ask authors to reach out to the publisher,

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:56.500
they have a very user friendly system they
can use to edit any of the citation data that

00:17:56.500 --> 00:18:02.289
